<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Dear {!Contact.FirstName},</font><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div><font face="arial"><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Thank you for your interest in graduate studies at the Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts School of Music at ASU. As one of the largest universities in the country, the ASU School of Music awards over $2 million to students annually, providing an excellent education at an unbeatable value. ASU's diverse and innovative community is a perfect complement to the personal attention you will receive in the School of Music. With a population of around 750 students, we offer small class sizes, state-of-the-art facilities and one-on-one instruction from world-renowned faculty. &nbsp;We invite you to consider the ASU School of Music for this important step in your music studies.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">If you are interested in applying for fall 2017 admission, please first contact the School of Music Admissions office at <a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">musicadmissions@asu.edu</a> to confirm that your desired program is accepting late applications. If you are interested in future study at ASU, please refer to the information below as a guideline for what to expect when you are ready to apply. For an idea of the course requirements for the various degree programs offered, select one of the checksheets accessible by your degree program of interest <a href="https://webapp4.asu.edu/programs/t5/programs/Keyword/music/graduate/false">here</a>.&nbsp;</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><a href="http://students.asu.edu/costs">Tuition and fees</a> at Arizona State University are reasonable, even for non-resident students. Music Scholarships and teaching assistantships are available. Typical assistantships are 25% which amount to 10 hours of work per week and receive:</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Tuition remission covering the non-resident portion of tuition</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">50% reduction in the resident portion of tuition (excluding fees)</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">$7,450 stipend for the academic year, distributed over bi-weekly paychecks</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Spoken English requirement</b>: If your native language is not English you must meet <a href="https://learnenglish.asu.edu/international-teaching-assistant">spoken English requirements</a></span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;before you can be considered for &nbsp;teaching assistantship. You may complete the ASU SPEAK test (minimum score of 55).Those wishing to be considered for Graduate Teaching Assistantships should submit a </span><a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-teaching-assistants" style="font-size: 12pt;">TA application</a><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> by <b>February 15</b> for an appointment beginning fall semester.&nbsp;</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>Application Process</b></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>Step 1</b>. You must first submit the Graduate Admissions application, followed by the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-steps-to-apply">School of Music</a> application, before an audition or interview will be scheduled.</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>Step 2</b>: All transcripts and test scores must be submitted directly to the Graduate Admissions Office of the University.</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>Step 3</b>: Auditions or Interviews will be scheduled and application materials will be reviewed only after all application materials have been submitted. We are not responsible for application materials sent to the wrong office or directly to faculty. Please check the <a href="http://graduate.asu.edu/">Graduate Education website</a> for application information, and the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-steps-to-apply">School of Music website</a> for specific application requirements for your degree program.</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>Applicants to the PhD Music Education, PhD Musicology, DMA Composition, and DMA Interdisciplinary Digital Media and Performance programs</b> must submit GRE scores. The GRE examination in Music is not acceptable for admission to the doctoral program. GRE scores must be from within 5 years prior to the first day of the enrollment term.</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Due to the high volume of applicants we receive each year, we recommend that you plan to apply as early as possible.</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-deadlines-fees" style="font-size: 12pt;">Application Deadlines</a></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b><br></b></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>Spring Admission</b>: The application deadline is <b>October 15 for all degrees</b> except for the following programs with prescreening requirements:</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">All voice concentrations</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">MM Composition</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">DMA Composition</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">DMA Interdisciplinary Digital Media and Performance</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">DMA Conducting</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">DMA Performance</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The deadline for the above listed programs is <b>October 1</b>.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>Fall Admission</b>: The application deadline is <b>December 1</b> for all degrees except for the following programs with rolling deadlines:</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">MM Music Education</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">PhD Music Education</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">MM Music Therapy</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Prescreening Materials</b>: Materials uploaded in the School of Music application and must be received by <b>October 1</b> for spring admission and <b>December 1</b> for fall admission. Please visit <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-auditions">this site</a> for more information.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-auditions">AUDITION DATES &amp; INFORMATION</a></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>Spring Admission</b>:</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Saturday, November 19, 2016 (flute applicants not accepted for spring admission)</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><b>Fall Admission</b>:</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Please review the <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-auditions">Graduate audition website</a> for dates specific to your instrument.</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">DMA applicants who are invited to audition after submitting prescreening materials must perform a live, on-campus audition. Recorded auditions are acceptable for master’s degree performance applicants only and must be uploaded <a href="https://music.asu.edu/admissions/graduate-recordings-portfolios">online</a> by November 1. CD/DVD audition recordings are not accepted. To be considered for a music scholarship or teaching assistantship, a live, on-campus audition is preferred.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ad hoc auditions may be scheduled with faculty (required for <b>organ</b> applicants), but must be completed by December 1 for spring admission and February 28 for fall admission.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Flute applicants are not considered for admission to any spring semester.</span></li></ul></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">We welcome you to contact us via email to </span><a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu" style="font-size: 12pt;">MusicAdmissions@asu.edu</a><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> if you have any additional questions. We also encourage you to refer to the School of Music Web site, </span><a href="https://music.asu.edu" style="font-size: 12pt;">music.asu.edu</a><span style="font-size: 12pt;">, as a resource for your admissions questions.</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Best wishes,</div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">Office of Admissions</div><div><font color="#990000"><b>School of Music</b></font></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><font color="#ffcc66"><b>Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts</b></font></span></div><div><font color="#990000"><b>Arizona State University</b></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font color="#ffcc33"><br></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><font><a href="https://music.asu.edu"><font color="#ffcc33">music.asu.edu</font></a> </font><font>|</font><font> <a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu"><font color="#ffcc66">musicadmissions@asu.edu</font></a></font></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><span style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: 12pt;">{!Case.Thread_Id}</span></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></div></font></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>